menu "Micro OS drivers"

config MICRO_OS_BUZZER_BEEP_ON_CHECK
	bool "Beep at boot to prove that the buzzer works"
	default n
	help
	  The hardware doctor sounds the buzzer for 30 ms at every boot,
	  so that the buzzer and its LEDC timer can be heard working.
	  The check itself does not need the sound - the state of the
	  module is the same either way - so the beep is off by default
	  and this switch brings it back.

endmenu
